---
description: Never ship visible stubs, orphan routes, or half-wired config/API surfaces
alwaysApply: true
---

# No unfinished surfaces

Ship **working** or **hidden** — never a user-visible placeholder that looks like a feature.

## Forbidden

- Tabs/pages that render "Coming Soon" / "not available yet" for users who already have permission
- Routes or nav links to stub pages when real UX exists elsewhere
- Orphan components/pages never imported (dead nav with wrong paths)
- API client methods for endpoints nobody calls (especially broken stubs)
- Config keys / OpenAPI routes with no implementation (e.g. payment keys, 501 social connect)
- Context providers that expose `showX` / `setX` but never render `X`

## Prefer

```text
Hide the tab / remove the route  →  until thin-wire is ready
Delete dead files                →  don't keep "maybe later" modules
Remove config + docs             →  or implement + test in the same change
```

## Tests

When hiding or removing a stub, update unit/e2e that asserted the placeholder in the **same** change. Prefer a cleanup gate test that the stub string / orphan path is gone.

## Backend counterpart

Do not keep `raise ValueError("retired")` service methods if HTTP already returns 410 — delete the dead methods and assert absence in tests.
